WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.085 --> 00:00:03.070
(Andy clapping)

00:00:03.070 --> 00:00:04.443
Yes.
Woo, woo!

00:00:04.443 --> 00:00:06.520
Woo-hoo, hoo!
Woo.

00:00:06.520 --> 00:00:07.983
Yes.

00:00:09.170 --> 00:00:10.840
Welcome to the show, everybody.

00:00:10.840 --> 00:00:13.520
A stellar program tonight.

00:00:13.520 --> 00:00:18.460
Hilarious comedian Beth Stelling
is going to be joining us.

00:00:18.460 --> 00:00:21.930
Also joining us, a packed house.

00:00:21.930 --> 00:00:26.630
That's right, we have a full,
full crowd again tonight,

00:00:26.630 --> 00:00:28.950
because as you probably know,

00:00:28.950 --> 00:00:32.540
we borrowed a page from
Major League sports,

00:00:32.540 --> 00:00:37.480
and we decided to fill our
audience with cardboard cutouts.

00:00:37.480 --> 00:00:41.550
You, the fans, sent us your photos,

00:00:41.550 --> 00:00:44.790
we printed them out, and here they are.

00:00:44.790 --> 00:00:49.650
We had close to 20,000
submissions, I think,

00:00:49.650 --> 00:00:51.450
and here we've packed the audience

00:00:51.450 --> 00:00:54.930
completely full, and fantastic.

00:00:54.930 --> 00:00:59.930
In fact, it's so full, that
we have a standby line.

00:01:01.850 --> 00:01:05.930
That's right, we have a standby
line outside the theater.

00:01:05.930 --> 00:01:08.940
Look at that, that takes dedication.

00:01:08.940 --> 00:01:13.370
Those are people, we have record
heat, record temperatures,

00:01:13.370 --> 00:01:16.200
those are people that are
braving those temperatures,

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:19.600
'cause cardboard is flammable.

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:22.810
They are braving those
temperatures outside.

00:01:22.810 --> 00:01:25.440
That's how popular this show is, Andy.

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:27.950
It's unbelievable.
We've got people outside.

00:01:27.950 --> 00:01:30.570
It's, we are, we are the number one show

00:01:30.570 --> 00:01:32.270
among the one dimensional crowd,

00:01:32.270 --> 00:01:34.220
I guess it's two dimensional.

00:01:34.220 --> 00:01:35.130
Yeah.
Yeah, yeah.

00:01:35.130 --> 00:01:37.980
No, among cardboard cutouts,
we are the number one show.

00:01:37.980 --> 00:01:40.020
Yup, we score very highly.

00:01:40.020 --> 00:01:42.060
Any interesting people around you

00:01:42.060 --> 00:01:43.310
that we should check out?

00:01:44.150 --> 00:01:47.730
Yeah, he, I'm not sure
he's loving the show.

00:01:47.730 --> 00:01:49.900
Yeah, but see with these two together,

00:01:49.900 --> 00:01:53.823
it's like, it tells a story
about somebody made a stinky.

00:01:54.680 --> 00:01:56.980
Okay (laughing).
See, he's like "Ew,"

00:01:56.980 --> 00:01:59.067
and she's like, "Oops."

00:01:59.067 --> 00:02:00.690
(Conan laughing)

00:02:00.690 --> 00:02:02.130
What about across the aisle, Andy?

00:02:02.130 --> 00:02:03.143
Who's over there?

00:02:04.100 --> 00:02:06.200
Oh my God, there's a beat poet.

00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:07.276
[Conan] Oh, look at that.

00:02:07.276 --> 00:02:08.320
Yeah. look at that guy.

00:02:08.320 --> 00:02:12.630
He got, I've heard his
poetry is very daring

00:02:12.630 --> 00:02:13.800
in the 1950s.
Yeah,

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:17.203
very confrontational and
he's ready to duke it out.

00:02:19.420 --> 00:02:21.340
There's a lady with a fancy hat.

00:02:21.340 --> 00:02:22.490
Oh, I like her hat.

00:02:22.490 --> 00:02:25.130
Yeah, we don't get too many
ladies with fancy hats.

00:02:25.130 --> 00:02:25.963
You know what I like?

00:02:25.963 --> 00:02:28.270
I like it, it's like the old
days when people dressed up

00:02:28.270 --> 00:02:29.350
to go to a taping.
Right,

00:02:29.350 --> 00:02:32.785
what's wrong with you, you dirty beatnik?

00:02:32.785 --> 00:02:35.640
(Conan laughing)

00:02:35.640 --> 00:02:37.623
Let's see what else we got back here.

00:02:40.075 --> 00:02:44.360
It looks like a, either a
paranoid or an eco-terrorist.

00:02:44.360 --> 00:02:46.070
I'm gonna go with eco-terrorist.

00:02:46.070 --> 00:02:47.363
Good, it's sexier.

00:02:50.690 --> 00:02:52.063
Let's see, okay.

00:02:53.320 --> 00:02:54.750
I'm against this.

00:02:54.750 --> 00:02:57.010
Do you think that guy is
pleasuring himself back there?

00:02:57.010 --> 00:02:58.600
I think he may be.

00:02:58.600 --> 00:03:00.410
I mean, it's hard with no arms,

00:03:00.410 --> 00:03:03.520
but he's still managing to do it.

00:03:03.520 --> 00:03:07.320
Well, let me say, I can
attest it can be done

00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:08.260
with no arms.

00:03:08.260 --> 00:03:10.010
(Andy laughing)

00:03:10.010 --> 00:03:12.390
And if you're gonna do it
with no arms, the back row

00:03:12.390 --> 00:03:14.360
is the best place to be.
It certainly is,

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:16.420
just 'cause of the noise.
Well, I am just so excited

00:03:16.420 --> 00:03:17.750
that not only are these people here,

00:03:17.750 --> 00:03:21.420
but as I said again, there's
a standby line outside,

00:03:21.420 --> 00:03:23.450
people who couldn't get into the theater,

00:03:23.450 --> 00:03:27.150
braving record LA temperatures,
waiting for a chance

00:03:27.150 --> 00:03:31.333
for someone here to die, I think.

